// .swift-format — the ChatBots Swift style for swift-format (audit A06).
//
// swift-format reads this JSON with `//` comments. Before it existed, `swift-format lint
// --recursive Sources Tests` reported 30,059 diagnostics against this repository's own
// code, 93% of them from two settings disagreeing with the house style. With it in place
// the same command reports 3,003. The settings below state that style; the residual is
// accounted for at the bottom of this file.
//
// No rule is switched off here. `rules` is omitted so every swift-format rule stays at
// its default.
{
  "version": 1,

  // Four-space indentation is what every file in Sources/ and Tests/ actually uses
  // (except the two generated files, which are written by tools/embed-*.py). swift-format
  // defaults to two spaces, and that mismatch alone accounted for 27,994 of the 30,059
  // baseline diagnostics. This is the single most important line in the file.
  "indentation": {
    "spaces": 4
  },

  // Tabs are not used in this codebase; the width only affects how a stray tab is counted.
  "tabWidth": 4,

  // 120 matches the `line_length` warning threshold configured in .swiftlint.yml, so the
  // linter and the formatter agree on where a line becomes too long. swift-format defaults
  // to 100; moving to 120 removed 1,672 baseline diagnostics. The 107 that remain are the
  // same over-length lines swiftlint reports: 104 are string content, 3 are code.
  "lineLength": 120,

  // The codebase wraps long calls and collection literals by hand and aligns continuation
  // lines under the opening delimiter (see DeviceProfiles.swift). `respectsExistingLineBreaks`
  // keeps swift-format from re-flowing those deliberate breaks; setting it to false would
  // rewrite large parts of the tree and is not this task.
  "respectsExistingLineBreaks": true,

  // Multiline collection literals in this codebase carry a trailing comma, which is why
  // .swiftlint.yml sets `trailing_comma: mandatory_comma: true`. Keep the two tools
  // pointing the same way.
  "multiElementCollectionTrailingCommas": true,

  // Blank lines inside braces are not indented. This is swift-format's default; stated
  // here so the choice is explicit rather than inherited.
  "indentBlankLines": false,

  // At most one blank line in a row. swift-format's default, stated for the record.
  "maximumBlankLines": 1,

  // Multiline strings (the embedded web assets in WebAssets.swift, the sample transcripts
  // in tests) are content, not code, and must not be re-flowed or re-wrapped.
  "reflowMultilineStringLiterals": "never"
}

// What the 3,003 residual diagnostics are, measured with this file in place:
//
//   2,253  Sources/ChatBotsCore/WebAssets.swift   generated by tools/embed-web.py
//      32  Sources/ChatBotsCore/NameLists.swift    generated by tools/embed-names.py
//   -----
//     718  this repository's hand-written code
//
// swift-format has no exclude list (unlike swiftlint's `excluded:`), so the two generated
// files cannot be kept out of `--recursive Sources Tests`; the 2,285 diagnostics they carry
// are an artefact of embedded HTML/CSS/JS written at column 0 and of generated name lists.
// The 718 in hand-written code are real, and are dominated by deliberate house style:
//   Indentation 311, AddLines 200 (several arguments per continuation line), LineLength 95,
//   DoNotUseSemicolons 49, RemoveLine 16, TrailingComma 15, Spacing 11,
//   AlwaysUseLowerCamelCase 9, TrailingWhitespace 6, OrderedImports 3,
//   NoAccessLevelOnExtensionDeclaration 3.
// They are left visible for whoever fixes style later; nothing here suppresses them.
